prompt:
Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96: Keeg of the Moonmorel Hex performing a one-handed TOMAHAWK dunk. Use the attached Keeg animation sheet only as an identity and art-style reference. Redraw fifteen distinct complete full-body poses in a strict five-column by three-row grid, row-major, with broad transparent gutters and outer margins. Every athlete stays fully inside their own cell at consistent scale and camera. No copied or merged figures; no borders, court, hoop, floor, shadows, effects, text, labels, teammates, opponents, ball, sphere, orb, prop, or equipment.

Keeg is a flamboyant adult human man with normal athletic human anatomy, black hair, a neat close black beard, and an expressive face. Keep his complete very tall ornate purple witch hat with silver trim and mushroom ornaments recognizable in all fifteen poses. He wears the layered purple/lavender/silver Moonmorel Hex athletic kit with matching belt and shoes. Preserve his human face, adult proportions, two arms, two hands, two legs, black hair, beard, hat height and ornaments, kit palette, and shoes. No monster anatomy, horns, robe, cape, staff, extra limbs, altered uniform, or missing limbs. Both hands are always empty: the game basketball is separately rendered and must never appear in the drawings.

This is a TOMOHAWK dunk, not a windmill or reverse dunk. Keeg gathers the invisible ball, plants and rises, cocks the ball-miming hand behind his head like a tomahawk while keeping the hat clear, then snaps that arm forward over the crown and dunks one-handed. Pose10 (zero-based) is the only release at simulation tick21: the palm is open and empty at full reach. Poses0–9 carry the invisible ball in a natural hand arc; poses11–14 are empty-handed follow-through, descent, landing and recovery. Keep the ball hand separated from the full hat silhouette: no hand or ball is drawn on top of the hat. Unique connected poses:
0 controlled right-facing approach;
1 gather the invisible ball at waist;
2 low two-foot plant, knees flexed;
3 jump and lift the ball-miming hand toward the rear shoulder;
4 airborne, elbow bent, hand cocks behind the crown without touching the hat;
5 maximum tomahawk coil, hand far behind head;
6 powerful high ascent, torso starts unwinding;
7 arm accelerates forward above the hat, never across its silhouette;
8 near full extension with the wrist above the crown;
9 final cock and body twist toward the rim;
10 single RELEASE at tick21: arm fully extended upward/forward, open empty palm;
11 empty-handed arm follows through toward the rim;
12 descending with legs tucked naturally;
13 controlled two-foot landing, knees flexed;
14 balanced recovery with hands empty.

Keeg approaches moving toward image-right. Keep the right-facing body direction consistent; make the tomahawk motion clear from the pose sequence rather than changing his identity or scale. Clean arcade-sprite illustration edges and true transparency throughout, no alpha haze, checkerboard, matte, speckles, background, or colored artifacts. Return only the sprite sheet.
